	(text "Click a box on the left to open its page. \"Contents\" and the page numbers at the bottom right of\nevery page lead back here and to each page.\n\nCyan lines are connections: wires and pin ends, all one width. A dot joins lines; a cross on a pin\nend means the pin is not connected. Pins connect by net labels (the boxed names): pins whose labels\ncarry the same name are on one net, on any page. [3/C4] after a label: page 3 carries that net too,\nits label in zone C4 (column 4, row C of the border). Click it to land on that label. No [page/zone]:\nthe net is on this page only. Click a part's reference to find its row in the parts list; the row's\npage/zone leads back. White: parts and their references. Grey: values, pin names, pin numbers.\nA dashed frame is a block of the circuit, titled at its top left. An amber K3 marks a Kleidos\naddition or correction: it leads to its row below; a dotted line is an added connection."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 45.085 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b7bfdd86-7a84-58a3-8fdd-6b9388a287b6")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 84.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5fb76c2e-6eda-588e-88f9-20e6af783368")
	)
	(text "Every part, pin and net of the CoreInk, with the values the vendor documents: connectivity\ndocumented from the vendor's public documentation, with Kleidos additions and corrections listed\non page 1 (M5Stack's one-page CoreInk schematic, coreink_sch.pdf, and its docs page; the datasheets\nand the Kleidos firmware each entry cites; README.md and netlist.yaml beside this file). Layout and\nsymbols are this project's. No footprints, no PCB, no part numbers beyond the documented ones.\nValues are as the vendor prints them (10K/1%, 105/6.3V). No part on the print is marked not fitted.\nReference designators are the vendor's, not renumbered. Where the print numbers no pins (passives,\ndiodes, transistors, keys, antennas, the buzzer), the pin names are ours: 1/2, A/K, B/C/E, G/S/D.\nNets the vendor left unnamed carry names of ours (U5_FB, EPD_SW...). The USB-UART bridge is the\nCP2104 the print shows; the docs say later units carry a CH9102, as the bench unit does (README.md).\nZones: columns 1-8 and rows A-F, 50 mm apart, printed in the border."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 88.605 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9f04a113-17b1-5e87-bfa8-6130a44e69b4")
	)
	(text "Kleidos additions and corrections"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 127.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "64a52672-bef2-5cc9-b6cc-f834e01aae4b")
	)
